<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- Feb 14-17.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- Feb 14-17.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the February 14-17 Presidents Day weekend box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		    Four-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Star Wars		 $21,370,589	 $98,631,380</p>
<p>2. Absolute Power	  $16,770,220	 $----</p>
<p>3. Dante's Peak	    $13,662,270	 $36,271,100</p>
<p>4. Vegas Vacation	   $12,837,927	$----</p>
<p>5. Fools Rush In	    $ 9,714,940	$----</p>
<p>6. That Darn Cat	    $ 6,424,617	$----</p>
<p>7. Jerry Maguire	    $ 5,205,845     $127,708,151</p>
<p>8. The English Patient    $ 4,585,551	$47,738,423</p>
<p>9. Shine			$ 3,515,584	$20,024,158</p>
<p>10 Scream		     $ 3,261,988	$79,108,017</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Wars&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Absolute Power,&quot; &quot;Fools Rush In&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Vegas Vacation&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;That Darn Cat&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Scream&quot; and &quot;The English Patient&quot; are released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney.</p>
<p>&quot;Shine&quot; is released by Fine Line Features, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
</text>
